# Line endings
#
# `text=auto` on its own normalises to LF *in the repository* but still lets
# core.autocrlf (true on this Windows dev box) rewrite the working tree to CRLF
# on checkout - which is what produced a screen of
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" on every git add.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF as well, so there is no conversion left to
# warn about. Attributes here override core.autocrlf, so the behaviour is the
# same on every machine regardless of local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly declare text files, so detection is never guessed for these.
*.py text diff=python
*.js text
*.css text
*.html text
*.json text
*.md text
*.txt text
*.ini text
*.sql text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.toml text
ollama/Modelfile text

# Binary: never normalise, never diff as text. `text=auto` detects most of these
# anyway; declaring them stops a stray heuristic from corrupting one.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.pkl binary
*.pt binary
*.bin binary
*.safetensors binary

# Deny checkout for Windows-specific filenames to avoid cross-platform issues
aux -text
prn -text
nul -text
com1 -text
lpt1 -text
